## 9. Recommendations

| Priority | Action | Addresses |
|---|---|---|
| Critical | Reset passwords of all 7 DCSync accounts; reset `krbtgt` twice with the replication interval between resets; rebuild trust in tickets | 003 |
| Critical | Remove replication rights from `svc-monitor`; audit who holds `Replicating Directory Changes (All)` | 003 |
| Critical | Disable and rotate local account `Steve`; deploy LAPS for local administrators | 004 |
| High | Re-enable Kerberos pre-authentication for `j.melnyk`; alert on any account with it disabled | 002 |
| High | Move `svc-backup` to a gMSA or a 25+ character password; enforce AES and disable RC4 via GPO | 001, 002 |
| High | Enable LSA protection (RunAsPPL), Credential Guard and the ASR rule "Block credential stealing from LSASS"; block ProcDump and `ncat` with WDAC/AppLocker | 004 |
| High | Restrict remote WMI/DCOM and SMB admin shares to admin hosts; limit workstation outbound traffic | 004 |
| High | Fix rule 100205: enable Sysmon ProcessAccess for `lsass.exe`, match `-ma` with PID and `GrantedAccess`, do not depend on the output filename | 004 |
| Medium | Narrow rule 100203 (require absence of a preceding TGS context or exclude Kerberoasting TGT requests) and test it against CASE-001 data | 001, 002 |
| Medium | Add Suricata signatures for AS-REP responses and DRSUAPI `DsGetNCChanges` from non-DC hosts; verify they load and match | 002, 003 |
| Medium | Enforce NTP across all VMs (79 s skew seen); record the offset in each case | 004 |
| Medium | Complete evidence records and custody entries (section 8); analyse `lsass.dmp` with `pypykatz` and list exposed account names | all |

