## 10. Limitations

- Password cracking results for the Kerberoasting and AS-REP hashes are not documented, so exposure is stated as "hash obtained", not "password recovered".
- The content of `lsass.dmp` and the payload of the `ncat` transfer were not analysed or captured.
- Alert-to-event matching was done for the case windows only. Earlier runs in the shared logs (from 06:41 UTC) were not analysed.
- SENSOR role and the VM-to-IP mapping other than DC01 are inferred from traffic.
- The Wazuh agent restart at 05:36:53 (CASE-004) may explain missed alerts for dumps #1 and #2, but this was not tested.

